⚠️ **IMPORTANT (carried over, unchanged from round 2): residual parser-order contamination — a path-bearing `##[error]path:line:` line inside an unterminated `[FAIL]` section is still swallowed with a mangled path and rendered as "foreign, do not chase"**

Re-verified on head `9f53070` — `extractViolations` still runs `genericErrorViolations` **last** (this line), so the narrow shape from the previous round reproduces byte-for-byte:

```js
extractViolations(
  '[FAIL] method_size: 1 violations\n' +
  ' a/one.dart:1: too big\n' +
  '##[error]lib/widgets/foo.dart:12: build failed', 'gate')
// → [
//   { rule:'method_size', path:'a/one.dart', line:1 },                              // correct
//   { rule:'method_size', path:'##[error]lib/widgets/foo.dart', line:12, ... }      // mangled
// ]
// tagOwnership with lib/widgets/foo.dart IN the diff → 'foreign' (do-not-chase bucket)
```

The `##[error]` prefix baked into the captured "path" fails the `sameFile` suffix check, so a genuinely owned error lands under **"Foreign / infra reds (do not chase)"** — the #433 pathology this PR exists to kill. The round-2 mitigations still bound the blast radius (the runner's `##[error]Process completed with exit code N.` line does not match the crap4j detail shape; `::error file=…,line=…::` annotations don't match either; the raw message still names the path in the foreign table), which keeps this non-blocking — same adjudication as the previous round.

The fix remains the same one-liner class as round 1 — claim the generic shape before the greedy section scanner:

```js
dartAnalyzeViolations(lines, checkName, taken, out);
dartTestViolations(lines, checkName, taken, out);
genericErrorViolations(lines, checkName, taken, out);   // ← before crap4j
crap4jViolations(lines, checkName, taken, out);
jscpdViolations(lines, checkName, taken, out);
```

(or terminate `currentRule` in `crap4jViolations` when a line starts with `##[` / `::`). Please add the regression fixture: a `[FAIL]` header followed by `##[error]<diff-file>:12: msg`, asserting the item's clean path and `ownership === 'owned'`.

